// The Go examples are written exactly as a consumer's module is: they `require` the
// published github.com/openmatter-network/matter-sdk-go, with no `replace` of their own.
// Inside this repository this workspace points that requirement at the sources next
// door, so CI builds the examples against the code under review. `GOWORK=off go build`
// builds them against the released module instead.
//
// The package is replaced, not `use`d: Go refuses to replace a workspace member at every
// version, and pinning one here would give the release version another home to drift in.
go 1.22

use (
	./client-go
	./go-e2e
)

replace github.com/openmatter-network/matter-sdk-go/v2 => ../packages/go/mattersdk
